WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.750
Embryology will lead you to seek honesty in your feelings.

2
00:00:09.340 --> 00:00:13.670
And that can be unsettling because we'll have to go into another context which is

3
00:00:13.670 --> 00:00:15.748
not a context where will can intervene.

4
00:00:19.300 --> 00:00:23.390
That is, I cannot have a pure voluntary act, I must be in an act of participation.

5
00:00:23.390 --> 00:00:25.910
Because the fetus developing there has power.

6
00:00:25.910 --> 00:00:28.580
It has power, it is very oriented, it makes very few mistakes.

7
00:00:28.580 --> 00:00:31.520
And finally, they still show us quite a few interactions,

8
00:00:31.520 --> 00:00:33.500
inductions and synchronicity in development.

9
00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:37.820
And we're going to study all that together, first through the very first movements.

10
00:00:37.820 --> 00:00:41.090
And we're going to look for certain algorithms through this development.

11
00:00:41.090 --> 00:00:44.460
That means things that are present and that can be repetitive,

12
00:00:44.460 --> 00:00:46.060
in which we can settle and work with.

13
00:00:46.060 --> 00:00:47.380
And so here we have...

14
00:00:47.380 --> 00:00:51.570
a small embryo, you see, with a neural tube and a cardio-pleuro-planetary cavity.

15
00:00:51.570 --> 00:00:53.910
And which we don't see in books, when we study anatomy,

16
00:00:53.910 --> 00:00:55.722
embryology, we don't see growth.

17
00:00:55.722 --> 00:00:57.055
And that gives us wrong perceptions.

18
00:00:57.055 --> 00:01:00.459
But if we look at how anatomy is really built, man is absolutely not built around a

19
00:01:00.459 --> 00:01:00.909
bone structure.

20
00:01:00.909 --> 00:01:04.489
Even though bone appears much later in development. So we don't build ourselves.

21
00:01:05.640 --> 00:01:07.480
from the dense, we build from the fluid.

22
00:01:10.580 --> 00:01:14.630
And if we go even further, we realize that where does the fluid come from,

23
00:01:14.630 --> 00:01:16.239
how does this fluid itself build?

24
00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:26.412
Well, we see that it comes from an almost electrical, almost electromagnetic level.

25
00:01:27.951 --> 00:01:30.871
And if we go further, ultimately, it's almost a photon level,

26
00:01:30.871 --> 00:01:33.471
luminous level, as if light could induce matter.

27
00:01:33.471 --> 00:01:34.821
It's a bit philosophical.

28
00:01:42.991 --> 00:01:45.411
That's really what I'm going to explain, actually.

29
00:01:45.411 --> 00:01:47.143
We're going to start from the first series.

30
00:02:54.422 --> 00:02:57.712
We see that the thing that develops here, it develops at the same time here.

31
00:03:01.102 --> 00:03:04.902
And we will see that we can even find synchronisms on molecular,

32
00:03:04.902 --> 00:03:05.941
cellular, tissue planes.

33
00:03:14.442 --> 00:03:19.762
In the peritoire, you have molecular synchronicities that will occur in cerebral processes. Or even...

34
00:03:21.672 --> 00:03:24.132
What will happen, for example, at the level of the crista galli,

35
00:03:24.132 --> 00:03:26.108
will happen at the same time at the level of the falx cerebri.

36
00:03:28.632 --> 00:03:32.472
For now, the only thing I'm asking you is to already see that there is growth.

37
00:03:38.432 --> 00:03:41.582
We will see the development from the first cell, from fertilization,

38
00:03:41.582 --> 00:03:44.937
and even what happens already before fertilization, on an electrical plane,

39
00:03:49.662 --> 00:03:53.572
until the appearance of a first median line, which we will call the notochordal

40
00:03:53.572 --> 00:03:55.002
axis, with the establishment.

41
00:03:55.002 --> 00:03:58.372
first of a fluid cavity, which will be your first peritoneal cavity,

42
00:03:58.372 --> 00:04:02.192
primitive, of an amniotic cavity, until the formation of a third chamber,

43
00:04:02.192 --> 00:04:05.882
which is called the vitelline cavity, then the appearance within an embryonic tissue

44
00:04:05.882 --> 00:04:09.202
of a movement, of a wave that will form the notochordal process,

45
00:04:09.202 --> 00:04:12.636
which will induce the neurological process and which we will study.

46
00:04:12.636 --> 00:04:14.103
all the dynamic development of the brain.

47
00:04:14.103 --> 00:04:17.903
And what is the practical implication that we will find each time in osteopathy?

48
00:04:17.903 --> 00:04:20.053
You understand what I mean, that there is no will.

49
00:04:20.053 --> 00:04:23.204
You're in the womb, it's developing, you can't say stop, wait.

50
00:04:25.393 --> 00:04:29.213
The thing grows completely. So we will be invited to participate on that level.

